/T (Since the diode is ideal, during the positive half cycle of the ac voltage, the diode will conduct and allow current to flow, charging the capacitor to the peak voltage of the ac source, which is 311 V. During the negative half cycle, the diode will be in reverse bias and will not conduct, thus isolating the capacitor and maintaining its charge. Therefore, the potential difference across the capacitor will be equal to the peak voltage of the ac source. Hence, the potential difference across the capacitor is:)
/E (Since the diode is ideal, during the positive half cycle of the ac voltage, the diode will conduct and allow current to flow, charging the capacitor to the peak voltage of the ac source, which is 311 V. During the negative half cycle, the diode will be in reverse bias and will not conduct, thus isolating the capacitor and maintaining its charge. Therefore, the potential difference across the capacitor will be equal to the peak voltage of the ac source. Hence, the potential difference across the capacitor is:)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [7]
>>
